WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.160
In life, respiration releases heat.

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.590
Your core stays near 37 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.380
After death, respiration stops.

4
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:13.440
No heat is produced, and the body
loses heat to its surroundings.

5
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.690
Bacteria from inside the
body begin their work.

6
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.030
And within minutes to
hours, blowflies arrive.

7
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.760
With no witnesses, what clues inside and
on a body reveal how long ago the person

8
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.790
died?

9
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.440
In this mission, you'll
read a cooling curve,

10
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.370
as a body's core temperature falls from
37 degrees Celsius towards that of the

11
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:35.610
air around it.

12
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.940
Then you'll follow a
blowfly from egg to adult,

13
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.090
one life stage at a time.

14
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.870
Your mission: find out which clues
reveal how long ago a person died.
